COSMIC greeter
==============

Enable the dbus, cosmic-greeter-daemon and cosmic-greeter runit services.
Disable any other display-manager service before enabling cosmic-greeter.

The greeter uses /etc/greetd/cosmic-greeter.toml; it does not replace greetd's
default configuration. The greeter account is _cosmicgreeter.

elogind is required for session management. It can activate through D-Bus;
running a separate elogind service is optional. PAM's system-local-login
stack registers sessions and creates the runtime directory.
